+    "caa9_key_findings_detailed": "Using normative models across IDPs and voxel-wise Jacobians, the study quantified individual deviation maps and extreme deviation counts. For 1q21.1 distal CNVs, some duplication carriers showed large negative deviations in cerebellum, brainstem, and pallidum, while some deletion carriers showed notable positive deviations in caudate and accumbens. Compared to the no-CNV cohort, CNV carriers’ extreme deviation counts often lay in the tails of the reference distributions. Across the cohort, total extreme negative deviations (z<-2) were modestly but significantly associated with lower general cognitive ability (Spearman r≈-0.04, P≈0.04), whereas extreme positive counts were not (r≈0.03, P≈0.09).",
